I"�<p>Come raise your glass in celebration, because how often does an author finish a trilogy? Some authors never have–and I’m one of them.</p>

<p>But Russell W. Johnson has climbed that mountain, reached that vaunted summit, set foot in that place only the brave may visit. He is one of a select few, a member of the elite cadre of artists who have completed a creative triptych and lived to tell the tale. And if we’re lucky, maybe we can coax him into telling it to us.</p>

<p>When and where? I’m so glad you asked! This Sunday, August 24th, at 2 p.m., come on down to Durham, NC’s newest bookstore, <em>Daughters Coffee &amp; Books</em>, and hear me pick Mr. Johnson’s brain. I know he’s got the goods, and frankly I plan to pick him up by the ankles and shake until every last one of his writing secrets comes rolling out for all of us to see.</p>

